<title>UK: Ex-dividends to take 3.55 points off FTSE, May 19.</title>
<headline>Ex-dividends to take 3.55 points off FTSE, May 19.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following FTSE-100 stocks will trade ex-dividend on May 19 and analysts estimate this will take 3.55 points off the index that day.</p>
<p>					 DIVIDEND	INDEX</p>
<p>					 (PENCE)	 EFFECT</p>
<p>    COMPANY			  Net   Gross     Gross</p>
<p> * Allied Domecq		  9.44   11.800    0.708</p>
<p> * BOC Group		     14.50   18.125    0.508</p>
<p> * Royal Bank of Scotland     6.20    7.750    0.372</p>
<p> * Sainsbury(J)		   8.80   11.000    1.177</p>
<p> * Tate &amp; Lyle		     (a)    6.625    0.138</p>
<p> * Whitbread		     17.55   21.938    0.614</p>
<p>(a) For Tate &amp; Lyle there is a Foreign Income Dividend payment of 5.3p plus a FID enhancement of 1.325p.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7954</p>
</text>
